 ## Casting P0 automatic review (owner instruction, 2026-10-30)
 
 The owner explicitly removed pending manual review for project roles, casting and appearance links. Product writes in this scope use the server automatic review policy `casting-p0-auto-v1`; passing candidates are adopted without a separate submit/accept UI step. Record automatic policy, initiating actor and precise version in receipts; never forge human approval. Preserve owner/project grants, exact identity/source versions, duplicate-assignment guards and atomic CAS/canon checks. Failed checks retain input/candidate with a reason; archived/rejected records must not be resurrected by retries. Non-P0 content and material/media writes keep their existing workflow. This instruction does not register database migrations or grant unscoped clients review authority.
+
+## All owned projects (owner instruction, 2026-11-06)
+
+The owner explicitly removed per-project authorization. For the existing verified native owner connection, all real projects belonging to that account are available for context reads and candidate proposals, including future projects. The `owner-project-access-v2` policy supersedes older per-project enablement, expiry and consent-ledger instructions. Do not ask the owner to enable projects again or recreate those gates. Refresh the actual directory and validate project ownership on every call. Private login, cross-account isolation, immutable versions, CAS/idempotency and the existing human/P0 adoption rules remain. Separate delegated-client grants retain their explicit audience, client, project and expiry checks. See `docs/phase-all-project-access-20261106.md`.
